# Prettier scope — see `docs/README.md` §2 for why the docs are excluded.
#
# Prettier's own default ignore already covers `.gitignore`, so `node_modules`
# and `dist` are handled there. This file exists for the two things that are
# tracked in git and would otherwise be reformatted by an editor's
# format-on-save, which does not read the npm script's globs.

# 1. Documentation.
# The canonical docs in `docs/` are approved artefacts. Prettier's only change
# to them is padding markdown table cells to a uniform width — the rendered
# output is byte-for-byte identical, so the entire diff is noise that would bury
# real content edits in review. `docs/_legacy/` is explicitly archived and
# non-authoritative; reformatting it is pure churn.
docs/

# 2. Vendored and generated code.
# `backend/.gitignore` excludes these, but Prettier only reads the root
# `.gitignore`, so they have to be named again here.
backend/vendor/
backend/storage/
backend/bootstrap/cache/
backend/public/
frontend/public/

# Lockfiles are machine-written; formatting them creates conflicts.
package-lock.json
backend/composer.lock
